  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="transcription" xml:id="transcription_aad_0177" xml:lang="en">
        <div type="letter">
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00530/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
          <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_black_salus">
            <opener>
              <seg>
                <placeName>
                  <address>
                    <lb/><space quantity="40" unit="char"/><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_668">749 Washington Street 
                    <lb/><space quantity="40" unit="char"/>New York 10014</rs>
                  </address>
                </placeName>
              </seg>
              <salute>
                <lb/>Dear <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">Wystan</rs>,
              </salute>
            </opener>
            <p>
              <lb/>I presume that you are now safely ensconced in <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_5">Kirchste<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_salus">ee</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_salus">tt</add></subst>en</rs>,
              <lb/>and are working hard.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I have been working on the <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_670"><rs ana="#ana_155">Lichtenberg</rs></rs>,
              <lb/>which I hope to finish before leaving for <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_30">Europe</rs> in late June,
              <lb/>and on the <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_444">Edda poems</rs>.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I have five or six of <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_671">Paul Taylor</rs>'s
              <lb/>versions in hand right now, and I hope to get them off to you
              <lb/>in a week or so.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>What I have are: <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_445">Skirnir's Journey</rs> (about
              <lb/>160 lines), <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_446">The Treachery of Asmund</rs> (about 100 lines), <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_447">The
              <lb/>Waking of Angantyr</rs> (120 lines), the <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_448"><foreign xml:lang="non">Vafthrúdnismál</foreign></rs> (200 lines),
              <lb/><rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_449"><foreign xml:lang="non">Grimnismál</foreign></rs> (220 lines), and <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_450"><foreign xml:lang="non">Eir<unclear>í</unclear><subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_salus">l</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_salus">k</add></subst>smál</foreign></rs> (31 lines).<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>This last
              <lb/>is not truly Eddic: it is one of the late poems that combines
              <lb/>Eddic and Skaldic tradition, but of these it is the only really
              <lb/>successful one, the only one that holds the metre.
            </p>
            <p>
              <lb/>I was up at <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_669">Amherst</rs> Monday, Tuesday and Wednesday of last
              <lb/>week, and spoke to some of the people on <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_405">MassReview</rs>.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>They are
              <lb/>very eager to have one or more of the poems, and so you might 
              <lb/>send me the <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_451"><foreign xml:lang="non">Havamal</foreign></rs> (when you finish it), and I'll forward it to
              <lb/>them.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>Otherwise, we might let them have some combination of
              <lb/>the six enumerated a<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_salus">v</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_salus">b</add></subst>ove.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>Perhaps, in view of its length, we
              <lb/>could let <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_672">Alexis</rs> have <rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_450"><foreign xml:lang="non">Eiriksmál</foreign></rs> for <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_406">QUEST</rs>.
            </p>
            <p>
              <lb/>I heard from <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_89">David Luke</rs> (from <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_1">Wien</rs>) yesterday, and he tells me 
              <lb/>that <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_407">Bantam Books</rs> is looking for someone to redo <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_673">Mann</rs>'s
              <lb/><rs type="lit_work" ref="#lit_work_id_452">Buddenbrooks</rs>.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I have told him that I would be very interested
              <lb/>in doing it, but that I don't think that Bantam -- from what I
              <lb/>know of their reputation -- would be willing to pay enough.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>It
              <lb/>is 700 pp. of difficult text, and I think I would have to ask
              <lb/>for 5000 for what I would imagine w<subst><del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_salus">i</del><add place="superimposed" hand="#type_black_salus">o</add></subst>uld be a good two-year job.
              <lb/>Please let me know what you think of this.
            </p>
            <p>
              <lb/>There seem to be a round of wedding in our circle this summer:
              <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_707"><rs ana="#ana_156">Emily Boothby</rs></rs> in <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_670">Strasbourg</rs> at the end of July and Wincie
              <lb/>Hannesson (from <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_391">Iceland</rs>) in <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_204">Edinburgh</rs> in September, and (not
              <lb/>to shock you too much) <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_674">Mary</rs> and <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_669">your most obt. and humble
              <lb/>servant</rs> in <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_122">Geneva</rs> the first week of July.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>(Yes, I am serious.
              <lb/>I have been thinking of it for some time, and we have now
              <lb/>decided and <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_671">Paul Taylor</rs> is arranging things.)
            </p>
            <p>
              <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_89">David</rs>'s letter, incidentally, was singularly Lukian -- he was
              <lb/>most worried about <rs type="event" ref="#amp_event_id_414">Greece</rs>, and your words about writing for the
              <lb/><rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_408">Observer</rs> on it did not quieten him at all.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I told him to go,
              <lb/>but I wonder if he will.
            </p>
            <p>
              <lb/>I, incidentally, have applied for the summer <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_409">Fulbrig<unclear>h</unclear>t</rs> to <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_391">Ice-
              <lb/>land</rs> for <del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_salus">the<space quantity="1" unit="char"/>yea<space quantity="1" unit="char"/></del> 1968, and hope to get it -- unless my Peace
              <lb/>activities stand in the way.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>I have still not gotten my learner's
              <lb/>permit <del rend="overtyped" hand="#type_black_salus">for</del> from the motor vehicles bureau, and I am beginning
              <lb/>to think that I never shall.
            </p>
            <closer>
              <salute>
                <lb/>Please give my love to <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_4">Chester</rs>, saving, of course, some for
                <lb/>yourself.
              </salute>
              <signed hand="#hand_red_salus">
                <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_669">Peter</rs>
              </signed>
            </closer>
          </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00531/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
          <div>
            <ab hand="#hand_blue_unident_0177">
              <lb/>47
            </ab>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
